  "solution": {
    "text": "Inter-molecular structure of Boric acid(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>BO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>) in solid phase:<br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/5cb217d3-5803-4534-ad6f-94eeac755ef6-22.PNG\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 270px;\" /><br />Boric acid has strong hydrogen bonding as we can see in the above figure, while <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BF</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;does not. Therefore boric acid is solid.",
